    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="0967" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A Pacific War/297: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-13">January 13,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received January 13—11:59 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>285. American interests—prisoners of war—China. Department’s 2761, December
                        7;<anchor n="85" xml:id="d814-f1"/> Legation’s 6036, December 21.<anchor
                        n="86" xml:id="d814-f2"/> Intercroixrouge, Geneva, writes January 11.</p>
                <pb facs="0968" n="956" xml:id="pg956"/>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Instructed Zindel, our delegate Hong Kong, visit four American aviators
                        reported prisoners Canton. Unfortunately visit impossible as activity
                        delegate now confined Hong Kong exclusively. Paravicini,<anchor n="87"
                            xml:id="d814-f3"/> Tokyo, requested intervene Japanese authorities
                        obtain authorization visit.”<anchor n="88" xml:id="d814-f4"/>
                    </p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d814-f1" n="85" xml:id="d814-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1942v01#pg_830">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 830</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d814-f2" n="86" xml:id="d814-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that the contents of No. 2761 had been transmitted to
                    Intercroixrouge on December 8, 1942 (740.00114A Pacific War/262).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d814-f3" n="87" xml:id="d814-f3-content">
                <p>F. Paravicini, International Red Cross Committee delegate to Japan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d814-f4" n="88" xml:id="d814-f4-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 1201, February 20 (740.00114A Pacific War/333), the Minister in
                    Switzerland reported that the aviators were interned at Shanghai. In telegram
                    No. 2102, April 3 (740.00114A Pacific War/390), he stated that a representative
                    of the Intercroixrouge on March 24 had visited the aviators in a
                    prisoners-of-war camp near Shanghai where they were reported as being in good
                    health and treated the same as other prisoners of war.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
